# Cost:         none in a normal build: only the selection is behind
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant,
#               `Sha256Compress::compress` calls the reshaped body, which a
#               differential test equates with the original.
# Upstreamable: no: the original is the clearer code; an extractor model of
#               the missing items makes the patch unnecessary.
# Drop when:    the extractor translates `transmute` between arrays of bytes
#               and the chunked iterators the original body uses.
# Test:         test p3-sha256 --lib hax_reshaped
# Mutation:     the reshaped body places the second half first, so it
#               disagrees with the original on every input with distinct halves.
#
# The original body reinterprets the two halves as one block with `transmute`, then writes each state word through `as_chunks_mut` zipped with the state.
# The reshaped body copies the halves into a block and writes the words by index.
# It calls the same `compress256` on the same block and initial state.
#
